From d46a992b6dfb01bf8c145cacc3a9c1f56069c7a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:56:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(zb_io): provide MacOS in the shim and name the API a
 formula lacks

Homebrew aliases OS::Mac as MacOS, and formulae such as sketchybar call
MacOS.version. The shim had no such constant, so the build died with a
raw Ruby NameError and a backtrace through the shim.

Add the alias, and report a NameError or NoMethodError from loading or
installing a formula as the name the formula needs and the formula line
that uses it. The backtrace is still printed when zb runs with -v.

Closes #348
